From f6aa01f9d74ef2da3eebed1ce4c6199099b255eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joan Torres Lopez <joantolo@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 11:49:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] remote-display-factory: Add CreateRemoteDisplay2 to maintain
 API stability

The previous change modified CreateRemoteDisplay's signature from taking
a simple remote_id parameter to a GVariant dictionary. This broke API
compatibility with existing clients.

To fix this, restore the original CreateRemoteDisplay method with its
original signature (taking remote_id as an object path), and add a new
CreateRemoteDisplay2 method with the enhanced properties dictionary.

Both methods call gdm_remote_display_factory_create_display() internally.
This maintains backward compatibility while providing new functionality
for clients that need to pass additional properties like hostname and
preauthenticated-user.
